<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Base (English) string catalog for the talkrypt Android app.

  Localization is backed by Android's resource system: every user-facing string
  the Context-ful UI layer renders goes through Loc.s(R.string.*) (see Loc.kt),
  which resolves against the device's current locale. To add a language, drop a
  res/values-<lang>/strings.xml with the same names translated (see values-es).

  NOT certified / NOT audited (project-wide). Security/disclaimer wording is
  preserved verbatim here and must be translated faithfully (never strengthened
  into a certification/compliance claim) in every locale.

  The deliberately UI-free shared model (ChatEvents.kt) produces short status
  lines in source-English by design (unit-tested headless on the plain JVM where
  no resource table exists; AndroidX-free precludes Robolectric). Peer message
  bodies are user-authored and never translated. See ChatEvents.kt for the note.

  Note: the brand name "talkrypt" is intentionally not translated.
-->
